# Coverage floor. May only RISE; the gate's `fix` half refuses to record a
# drop (SPEC.md V27). Raised from 0.0 at the scaffold to 99.17.
#
# EVERY LIBRARY SOURCE LINE IS EXECUTED. `cargo llvm-cov --show-missing-lines`
# reports uncovered lines in exactly one file: `src/main.rs`. The per-file
# text reports show zero uncovered lines in classify.rs, cli.rs, config.rs,
# corpus.rs, scan.rs and statement.rs. The small residue the merged summary
# still attributes to cli.rs and scan.rs is lib-vs-bin instantiation
# accounting, not source anyone can reach.
#
# The remaining 11 lines are `fn main`: reading argv, the working directory
# and HOME, then calling into `cli`. A binary entry point cannot be called
# by a unit test, so those lines are unverifiable rather than unverified.
#
# THEY ARE DELIBERATELY NOT EXCLUDED from the measurement. Passing
# `--ignore-filename-regex 'src/main\.rs'` would report 99.78 and would
# also remove the only pressure keeping main.rs thin -- code moved there
# would stop counting against this number, which is precisely the incentive
# that put 37 lines in it before. Leaving the gap visible is what keeps the
# binary an edge instead of a hiding place.
#
# Three earlier rounds were REFACTORS rather than new tests, and each was
# the right fix on its own terms:
#   * dispatch moved out of main.rs -- a binary's logic is untestable
#   * `perform` returns u8, not ExitCode -- ExitCode has no comparison, so
#     tests could call every arm and assert nothing
#   * `Matcher` replaced `GlobSet` -- `GlobSetBuilder::build()` is fallible
#     but cannot fail after per-glob validation, so three lines of error
#     handling existed that no test could reach. Removing the unreachable
#     branch beat explaining it.
#
# The floor RISES WITH THE CODE, and the gate enforces that rather than
# asking politely (V27). A rise of more than 0.5 above this number FAILS
# the coverage step; `hk fix --all` records it and clears the failure.
#
# That enforcement was missing until it was tested. hk runs a step's `fix`
# only when its `check` FAILS, so a rise -- which passed -- never reached
# the code that records it, and the message printed on a rise named a
# command that does not exist. The floor would have drifted further below
# reality with every well-tested commit, protecting less and less while
# reporting green.
#
# Do not raise this by excluding files.
#
# Besides `fn main`, THREE lines in the crate are uncovered, all in
# `ledger.rs`: the `Encode` error arm and its Display. `toml::to_string_pretty`
# is fallible, and on a fixed struct of Strings and integers it cannot fail.
# Unlike the `GlobSet` case -- where swapping to an infallible API deleted the
# branch -- there is no infallible TOML serializer to swap to, and swallowing
# the error would mean writing an empty ledger over a real one. So it stays,
# and the floor sits fractionally above measured coverage rather than being
# hand-lowered to match. The 0.3 fall margin absorbs that.

# RE-MEASURED 2026-08-24, after the mood signals, the runner move and the
# first three extractions: 99.21, against this floor of 99.26.
#
# The paragraph above is now STALE in its accounting and is kept because
# the argument still holds. It said three uncovered lines, all in ledger.rs
# around `Encode`. Those are now COVERED: `toml::to_string_pretty` is
# fallible after all -- it refuses a bare `f64::NAN` -- so the arm and its
# Display are reachable from a test, and `record_fire` against a directory
# reaches the open-error arm the same way.
#
# WHAT IS UNCOVERED NOW, all of it unreachable rather than untested:
#   * src/main.rs, 11 lines -- the binary entry, per the argument above
#   * src/cli/apply.rs, 6 -- the tty prompt (V20); there is no tty in a test
#   * src/ledger.rs, 4 -- `write_all` failing on a handle that OPENED, which
#     needs a full filesystem, and one brace
#   * src/runner.rs, 3 -- `try_wait` and `wait_with_output` returning an OS
#     error, plus a line in an assertion message
#   * src/cli.rs, 3 -- `itok` absent from PATH, and the no-roots return that
#     an earlier resolve error reaches first
#
# The floor STAYS at 99.26. It may only rise (V27), and lowering it to match
# a measurement is the ratchet filing its own teeth. The 0.3 fall margin was
# put here for exactly this residue.

# RE-MEASURED 2026-09-05, after `issue`, the check split and the guard:
#   99.07, against this floor of 99.26.
#
# THE FLOOR DOES NOT MOVE. It may only rise (V27), and lowering it to meet
# a measurement is the ratchet filing its own teeth -- the 0.3 fall margin
# exists for exactly this residue and this sits 0.19 inside it.
#
# The new code is FULLY covered: `src/issue/`, `src/cli/issue.rs` and every
# file of the `check` split report zero uncovered lines. What moved the
# number is the DENOMINATOR -- the crate grew by around 700 covered lines
# while the unreachable residue stayed where it was, so the same handful of
# lines is now a larger fraction of a bigger total.
#
# The residue itself is unchanged in KIND: the binary entry, the tty prompt
# V20 requires, OS errors on handles that opened, and `itok` absent from
# PATH. Nothing was excluded and nothing stopped being asserted.



# RAISED 2026-09-06, 99.26 -> 99.33, and MET for the first time since it was
# written. The two entries above record the floor standing above the
# measurement -- 99.07 against 99.26 -- deliberately, with the 0.3 fall margin
# absorbing the difference rather than the number being lowered to fit.
#
# WHAT WAS COVERED, all of it reachable and none of it excluded: `session_path`
# picking the newest transcript under a real root and the error when every root
# is empty; `catch` dispatching through the same seam as the other reporting
# verbs; `load_corpus` on a config that names no root; `plan` and `revert`
# refusing a `~` path with HOME unset, which is the same rule at both ends;
# `publish_artifact`'s two ways out before any filesystem work; `unpublish` on
# a rule and on a skill with a live link; `save` on a ledger path that cannot
# be written; a content shape `catch` does not know; a parentless path in the
# index test; and the class-moved arm of `show`'s ledger lookup.
#
# Two dead assertion arms went with them -- a `let ... else` and a loop body
# that could not run -- because an unexecutable assertion is not coverage owed,
# it is a test saying nothing.
#
# THE RESIDUE IS UNCHANGED IN KIND, and is what the remaining gap is: the
# binary entry, the tty prompt V20 requires, `Unimplemented` (kept on purpose
# for the day section I names a verb before this build performs it), OS errors
# on handles that opened, and `itok` absent from PATH.

